  "body": "After trying to stub `fetch()` in some unit tests [in this project](https://github.com/gaia-components/serviceworkerware), I came across that `bodyUsed` wasn't what I expected. I thought it was a boolean showing that the response contained a body, instead of a value telling that the body has already been used somewhere in your own code.\n\n[As the specs](https://fetch.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-response) are currently not very explanatory on that particular subject:\n\n> The bodyUsed attribute's getter must return true if the used flag is set, and false otherwise.\n\nI'd suggest to rename `bodyUsed` to `bodyAlreadyUsed`, to make the intent clearer.\n\nWhat do you all think?\n",
